A||||13||Steven||Engine/Trans Mounts||||1||
Z||000000||Steven||06-05-2001||11:51 AM||||Well the engine is about ready to go back in, and I just changed all the mounts. I was wondering which mounts showed the most wear on other peoples cars. Mine was the engine front mount, and I think what kill the one the most was the worn out rubber bushings in the dog bone. My car has the v-6 with a 4sp trans.<P>------------------<BR> 85 Fiero GT<BR> 3.2 Liter Under Construction||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GTZ34||06-05-2001||12:41 PM||||Steven,<BR>  I have an '87 V6 w/ auto.  I bought the car in late Feb and all of the mounts were shot. This was due to the hack job the previous owner's mechanic did on the car.  It didn't have a thermostat in it and a few other rigs causing it to run rich.  The cat was totally burned out and in doing so melted all (and I mean all) of the rubber from the front trans mount.  After that all of the other mounts failed due to the amount of engine movement.  So I guess what I am saying is that if you have mount failure for very long the other mounts will also be affected.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steven||06-05-2001||01:24 PM||||I guess that I was just surprized to see the trans mounts in good shape, and the front engine mount and dog bone bushing in such bad shape. I also replace the dampner (the little shock absorber thing), even thought it looked ok. Anyone else replace their mounts and found one that was much worse than the other?<P>------------------<BR> 85 Fiero GT<BR> 3.2 Liter Under Construction||||reg||1
Z||000003||hyhy4u||06-05-2001||03:35 PM||||I got a 87 GT with a Auto and 113k on it, the only thing i had to replace in that area was the dogbone, everything else is in great shape.||||reg||10
Z||000004||Steven||06-05-2001||03:55 PM||||Hyhy4u,<BR>How bad was your dog bone. Mine was torn up pretty bad in both rubber bushings. <P>------------------<BR> 85 Fiero GT<BR> 3.2 Liter Under Construction||||reg||1
Z||000005||DecadenceR||06-05-2001||04:05 PM||||From what I've been told, it's the dogbone mount that keeps the others from going bad as fast. And I know from experience that if that one mount is bad, there's a LOT of movement in the motor.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||06-05-2001||04:09 PM||||so where do you get them anyway - my dog bone looks a little chewed up - anybody know the GM part number for the V6 '85 dogbone?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Steven||06-05-2001||04:15 PM||||GM # 10046818. You can also get them from the Fiero Store with poly bushings, or just the bushing to replace the rubber in you old bone. That is the way I went.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DecadenceR||06-05-2001||04:33 PM||||I bought the poly / steel dogbone from the fiero store. Under $50 and worth it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Steven||06-05-2001||04:56 PM||||I looked at that, but figured the bushings do all of the real work, and so I just bought the poly bushings for my factory dog bone. Is the Fiero Store's dog bone polished or painted black? Just wondering after seeing all the engine pics from Dell today.<P>------------------<BR> 85 Fiero GT<BR> 3.2 Liter Under Construction||||reg||1
Z||000010||DecadenceR||06-05-2001||05:09 PM||||Yes, it's painted gloss black. Looks real pretty coming out of the box... LOL<BR>The reason I took the welded steel over the inserts was that I heard about the aluminum on the original mounts cracking because the poly doesn't flex as much as the original rubber, and the metal takes more abuse. And I know on my dad's old Chevy Celebrety when his mount went bad, the aluminum snapped in 3 places. So I just didn't want to have to do the job again down the road. I like paying for things once. Just in case...||||reg||1
Z||000011||Steven||06-05-2001||05:23 PM||||WOW!!! I had never heard of that happening before. Not much I can really do about it now except to keep an eye on the metal part of the bone, and keep the charge card handy. Thanks for the input on that.<P><BR>WOO-HOO post 150! Next stop 151.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Steven (edited 06-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Leadfoot||06-05-2001||06:02 PM||||When I tore out my engine I notice that the rear transmission mount was shot.  It was really gummy.  I guess all that oil leaking from the tranny softened it up. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||DecadenceR||06-05-2001||06:07 PM||||Well I know my dad's broke because the rubber was bad for a while, and he likes to take off really quick from a stop.<BR>I just didn't want to be a second case, if ya know what i mean!!!||||reg||1
